{
  "id": 211266307,
  "iid": 10048,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "wiretap: fix some narrowing warnings.",
  "description": "Make the protocol names passed to wtap_buffer_append_epdu_tag() static\narrays, so we can use sizeof to compute the string length; this should\nkeep at least some compilers from warning about a narrowing, as they can\ndetermine at compile time that the length fits in 16 bits.\n\nTo prevent other warnings, make the data argument to\nwtap_buffer_append_epdu_tag() const.  It's not modified, and it\n*shouldn't* be modified, so make it const so that you can pass pointers\nto const values to it (and so that somebody has to un-constify it if\nthey change wtap_buffer_append_epdu_tag() so as to break the contract).",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2023-03-14T23:13:58.004Z",
  "updated_at": "2023-03-15T00:50:43.241Z",
